{#
  Site-wide breadcrumb trail: "Nf3t's Vintage Story Wiki / <Section>" on every listing page, or
  "Nf3t's Vintage Story Wiki / <Section> / <item display name>" on every paginated detail page. This is
  the one shared place that generates the trail -- it replaces the old one-off
  `<div class="breadcrumb"><a href="...">&larr; All X</a></div>` back-links that used to be
  hand-rolled per template (see e.g. the old items.njk/structures.njk/etc.); don't reintroduce
  that pattern, call this macro instead.

  Call with `lang` (the global `lang` value) and `crumbs`, an array of `{label, url}` objects for
  every segment *after* the home link, which this macro always renders itself (linking to
  `('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url`, labeled "Nf3t's Vintage Story Wiki"). `url`, when present, is a path
  relative to the lang root (e.g. "items/", matching the same idiom every other internal link in
  this codebase uses) and renders as a link; the one entry with no `url` renders as the final,
  unlinked "you are here" segment:
    - A listing/index page passes a single `{label: "<Section>"}` entry (2-level trail: home +
      the current section, unlinked since it's the current page).
    - A paginated detail page passes the ancestor section as `{label: "<Section>", url: "<section>/"}`
      followed by `{label: <item's own display name>}` with no url (3-level trail).
#}
{% macro trail(lang, crumbs) %}
<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}">Nf3t's Vintage Story Wiki</a>
  {% for crumb in crumbs %}
    <span class="breadcrumb-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    {% if crumb.url %}<a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}{{ crumb.url }}">{{ crumb.label }}</a>{% else %}<span class="breadcrumb-current">{{ crumb.label }}</span>{% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
</nav>
{% endmacro %}
